CopyOnWriteArrayList
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Initialization:

At application startup, load the product catalog from the database into a CopyOnWriteArrayList<ProductDTO>.
Create a dedicated service (ProductCatalogService) to manage the product catalog.
Read Operations (Concurrent Access):

When a user requests the product catalog (e.g., browsing product listings, searching for products), the ProductCatalogService retrieves the data from the CopyOnWriteArrayList.
Multiple threads can concurrently read from the CopyOnWriteArrayList without any locking or contention, ensuring high performance.
Iterators over the CopyOnWriteArrayList are thread-safe and do not throw ConcurrentModificationException, even if updates occur concurrently.
Update Operations (Infrequent Updates):

When an administrative action or a scheduled batch job triggers a product update, the ProductCatalogService performs the following steps:
Retrieves the updated product data from the database.
Creates a new CopyOnWriteArrayList<ProductDTO> with the updated data.
Atomically replaces the old CopyOnWriteArrayList with the new one.
While the update is in progress, read operations continue to use the old CopyOnWriteArrayList, ensuring uninterrupted service.
Once the update is complete, subsequent read operations will use the new CopyOnWriteArrayList.
Simulating High Concurrency (Testing):

Use a tool like JMeter or Gatling to simulate thousands of concurrent user requests to the product catalog.
Monitor the application's performance (latency, throughput, CPU usage) to ensure it can handle the load.
Simultaneously trigger product updates to verify that read operations remain unaffected.


